# Build output. Non-negotiable: a release build of this workspace is
# ~500 MB of target/, and templedb's importer walks the tree — letting it
# in would put build artifacts in content_blobs, which is already the
# largest table in the database at 470 MB.
/target/
**/target/

# Rust/Cargo
Cargo.lock.bak
*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Nix
result
result-*
.direnv/

# The project's own Postgres cluster used to live at /.pgdata/ and no
# longer does — `just pg-up` puts it under $XDG_DATA_HOME. Kept as a
# belt-and-braces entry for anyone running from a git checkout, but note
# that this line is NOT what protects the database from the importer:
# TempleDB's scanner only honours .gitignore when the tree is a git
# repo, and an edit workspace is not. Four cluster config files reached
# content_blobs that way before the cluster was moved out of the tree.
/.pgdata/
